yep it happened guys and the memes  aren't lit the twitter board has finally  sold to elon for a whopping 44 billion  dollars so as the dust settles i wanted  to make a quick video recapping the  timeline of events and more importantly  look at the changes that elon plans to  make in the social media platform that  we all love and hate at the same time so  strap in this is going to be quite a  ride a timeline of events if you haven't  been living under a rock for the last  month then you'd be aware that the  mercurial billionaire we all love on  this channel has been on a crusade to  acquire twitter then out of nowhere elon  purchased nine point two percent of  twitter shelling out around three  billion dollars of his own pocket the  next day parag agarwal the ceo of  twitter tweeted out that he had welcomed  elon to join the board of directors but  in a major reversal on the 10th of april  the twitter board rejected this idea no  one was sure what led to that decision  still i suspect it had something to do  with elon sending out a series of  unusual tweets and polls about the  company that painted it in a bad light  then a few days later on the 14th of  april elon surprised us again when he  tweeted out that he had offered to buy  100 of the platform this announcement  led to the twitter board to scramble  screaming a hostile takeover all this  brings us to the present and after a  week of negotiations it was announced  that twitter would sell to elon and he  will take the company private by the end  of 2022 but after hearing all this you  might wonder what is elon's plan for the  platform so i want to cut through all  the political and philosophical chatter  around free speech and just focus on the  new features you and i may be seeing on  twitter soon and no it doesn't involve a  new like button in the shape of a tesla  icon for people following elon on  twitter he has laid out a lot of  breadcrumbs for us to pick up over the  years broadly elon wishes to undertake  four major changes to make the platform  better so let's unpack them one by one  the edit button first and foremost is  the inclusion of an edit button you me  and the weeknd all want the edit button  for that little mistake that gives that  tweet a whole new meaning live instead  of love licked instead of locked and  duck instead of anyways currently the  way twitter is set up doesn't allow you  to edit your tweets once you have posted  them so twitter has been toying around  with the idea of including an edit  feature for a long time however its  implementation will come with a whole  host of challenges this seemingly simple  change to the product will require  careful thought imagine someone tweets  something shocking and later decides to  edit it to make it more palatable but  users would have already responded to  the initial tweet and the damage would  have already been caused a later reddit  would lead to more confusion now granted  that most users would probably not use  this feature for the wrong reasons but  what do you do about the bad apples  people who are specifically using  twitter for nefarious purposes how do  you code for honesty one obvious  solution is to create an edit log like  facebook that lets people see the  history of all the changes but scammers  have abused this feature to con people  and spread disinformation on facebook so  elon and the engineers at twitter have a  lot of careful thinking to do if this is  to be a success maybe they decide to use  an ai to track the context behind each  tweet and intervene if someone tries to  change it too much or limit the time a  user has to edit the tweet after hitting  send just like the undo feature of gmail  either way twitter will most likely test  this new edit feature among users of  twitter blue its paid subscription  service before rolling it out to the  general audience and thanks to  alessandro palozzi who is considered a  leaker in the big tech community we now  have a pretty good idea of how twitter's  edit button might work if you look at  alessandro's leaks twitter has already  decided to incorporate multiple sub  features like maintaining an edit log  only letting people edit their tweets a  limited number of times giving users  only 30 minutes to edit their tweets and  displaying an edited mark next to the  tweet opening up the twitter algorithm  the second most important change that  elon wishes to bring about is to open up  the twitter algorithm so that users know  how tweets get recommended to them  according to elon twitter is way too  important and influential in today's  world to keep functioning behind closed  doors and trust me i've seen the social  dilemma and i think he's right twitter  users should be able to see how the  platform works and maintains complete  transparency in its operations this  means that it will allow users to see  how their tweets rank how they get  distributed to other users and whether  some have been demoted or promoted by  the twitter algorithm leaving no room  for behind the scenes manipulation in  addition it will allow users to  understand the factors that may increase  or reduce the visibility of their tweets  and use that knowledge to grow their  influence on the platform elon has even  suggested that twitter post the entire  source code on github so that  independent developers can look for  errors and suggest changes i believe  this is his way of creating a free open  source developer community around  twitter that will constantly give inputs  and ideas to the company on how to make  the platform better however i'm not sure  how he wishes to implement all this  because despite the user suggestions the  control of the code will still be in the  hands of the twitter executives making  accepting and not accepting the  suggested changes somewhat arbitrary  furthermore the twitter algorithm is  just the tip of the iceberg the main  power of any social media platform lies  in the data side of things so many  experts have argued that even if the  source code is made public it will be  totally useless without the inserted  data which contains plenty of private  and personal information in an exciting  twist of events according to disclose tv  some twitter employees trolled elon's  idea by adding a public repository on  the company's github page they called it  the algorithm and quickly removed it  before the source code was locked again  this has opened up a whole can of worms  for elon which i'm sure he wants to do  without as the company's new owner  anyway suppose he manages to implement  this properly in that case it will still  be a significant step towards  decentralizing a social media platform  we as users hardly know anything about  any other social media platform's  back-end algos so it'll be nice to see  someone changing that status quo  authenticating all humans the third  thing on elon's list is authenticating  all human users he has commented that he  wants to increase trust on the platform  and authenticating all human users is  how he wants to go about it not a lot is  known about how he wishes to implement  this feature but one possible way would  be to extend twitter's verification  system denoted by the blue tick next to  a user's name currently this  verification is available only to a  small group of people who have to meet  twitter's stringent criteria but this  feature can be opened up to the rest of  the twitter community in addition those  who are willing to back up their profile  with proof of identity such as a  passport should have the option to do so  however there are some problems  associated with this as well first of  all it will definitely dilute the  importance of the blue tick that most  political commentators journalists and  celebrities covered secondly there are  major concerns regarding user privacy  since verification of this kind will  require access to sensitive personal  information now we are already used to  sharing our personal data with private  entities but there are many people these  days who fear for their data privacy and  would like to keep away from the  platform if this becomes a mandatory  thing furthermore there are plenty of  valid reasons why some users may choose  not to use their real names or give  their personal information suppose they  are dissidents from an authoritarian  regime or repressed employees looking to  whistleblow on their company's  malpractices what does twitter do then  suppose they allow verified and  non-verified profiles in that case they  will create a tiered system of accounts  which doesn't really solve the problem  entirely some have even suggested that  elon authenticates humans using nft  profile pictures and blockchain  technologies i'm not sure how that will  work exactly but we can be sure that it  will not be easy for elon to fix this  problem overnight removing all the spam  bots the fourth and final thing that  elon wishes for is to divert company  resources to root out all the scammers  and bots that have plagued twitter over  the years in various tweets and speeches  elon has always highlighted this problem  according to him it is the single most  annoying problem on twitter and he is  right i absolutely hate hate those bots  spambots have always existed on twitter  but these days there has been a rise of  crypto scammers on the platform they  seem to have a free reign on almost  every thread they flood user feeds to  lure unexpecting victims and a lot of  people have become prey to this twitter  already had a sophisticated way of  weeding out these spam bots by detecting  various automation patterns but the  scammers have always been a step ahead  of them they have become increasingly  slippery allowing them to pass through  twitter's filters undetected it is even  more challenging to detect manual fakes  which are human beings creating fake  profiles to spam and i think that  perhaps the point of authenticating all  humans would help in detecting fake  accounts according to one of elon's  latest tweets twitter engineers under  him will focus on taking care of  spambots and scammers once and for all  or die trying he believes that he can  use a combination of human  authentication and advanced ai to  eliminate these bots but the challenge  will be in differentiating between  automated bots and humans who act like  bots on twitter whichever way he chooses  to implement it if he successfully makes  twitter bot free i am sure that it will  be a safer experience for all users why  has elon's twitter acquisition drawn so  much commentary although twitter's  business model has barely changed in the  last 10 years and the platform has  failed to keep up with its competitors  like facebook or tick tock when it comes  to rolling out new and improved features  to its audiences yet it still somehow  manages to be synonymous with public  discourse it has become the de facto  medium for all our culture war debates  and it remains a pulpit from which  influential people all over the globe  communicate with the masses i believe  this is what attracts elon to it it is  less of a business decision for him and  more of an investment into humanity's  future he wants to see twitter become a  maximally trusted and broadly inclusive  platform in his own words which can  attract the brightest minds to freely  debate humanity's most challenging  problems in his mind he is working  towards a civilizational goal in a world  that is becoming increasingly regulated  and polarized whether he manages to  transform the platform into a  civilization-defining company like  spacex or tesla or whether it ends up  becoming a mere tool for himself and  others to continue influencing their  vast audiences without any interference  remains to be seen if you enjoyed this  video do give it a thumbs up and  subscribe to the channel if you haven't  already see you in the next one

